  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0008_eeadbe416e90.png\" style=\"width:1.82708in;height:1.22708in\" /><br />Let feet of altitudes through <math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></math> are <math><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></math> respectively.<br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>C</mi></math> lies on the line <math><mi>C</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> &amp; <math><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></math><br />Now, the slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;the slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> <math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> equation of <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />Now, the slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>E</mi></math> is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;the slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> equation of the line&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Point of intersection of <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;gives point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
